abstract: >-
  Feasibility studies of vehicle-integrated photovoltaics usually treat the whole solar skin
  as a horizontal roof that is never shaded. SOLARIS-Twin extends the SOLARIS energy-balance
  toolkit for a 2.5 t seven-seat electric vehicle with a lidar-built digital twin of central
  Phoenix, Arizona: traffic-simulated trips, five parking sites and per-facet shading of an
  11.6 m2 PV skin over a typical year, cross-checked against a Unity ray-casting twin,
  SOLWEIG and street-level imagery. This release is the code and data pipeline of the
  journal manuscript submitted to the IEEE Transactions on Transportation Electrification.
keywords:
  - vehicle-integrated photovoltaics
  - solar electric vehicle
  - digital twin
  - urban shading
  - energy self-sufficiency
